\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Counting-basis matrices for scalar transport}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In the ascending vertex indicator basis, the counting adjoint of
[scalar transport](fdip-000Y) is the transpose array. The groupoid
identity is #{Q_y=P_gQ_xP_g^T}. The retained/eliminated split is
##{Q_x=\begin{pmatrix}A&H\\H^T&C_D\end{pmatrix},}
and the Schur complement in that basis is
#{S_R(x)=A-HC_D^{-1}H^T}. The same transcription writes
#{P_R^T} for #{P_R^{\dagger}} and #{H^T} for #{H^{\dagger}}. The values
#{19/105}, #{26/105}, #{3/8}, #{7/18} and #{1/72} are calculated
in the proof. So are the opposite-pair arrays #{A=C_D=dI_2} and
##{H=-\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\b&a\end{pmatrix}.}}
